# =============================================================================
# wire.sha256 — pinned Square Wire compiler for core/VERSIONS::WIRE_VERSION
# =============================================================================
# Read by idl/codegen/bootstrap_wire.sh. One line:
#
#     <sha256>  wire-compiler-<version>-jar-with-dependencies.jar
#
# published at
# https://repo1.maven.org/maven2/com/squareup/wire/wire-compiler/<version>/.
#
# Version-scoped on purpose: bumping WIRE_VERSION without refreshing this file
# leaves the bootstrap with no checksum for the JAR it is about to download, and
# it refuses to install an unverified compiler. Wire's output filenames change
# between releases (5.x renamed LoRAState.kt to LoraState.kt), so the version
# and its provenance must move together.
#
# To refresh after a bump:
#   v=<new version>
#   curl -fsSL -O "https://repo1.maven.org/maven2/com/squareup/wire/wire-compiler/$v/wire-compiler-$v-jar-with-dependencies.jar"
#   shasum -a 256 wire-compiler-$v-jar-with-dependencies.jar
# =============================================================================

69633e6fdc9a9bce51992804caebcd3be2218957092548162e73f114d9a407f1  wire-compiler-5.5.1-jar-with-dependencies.jar
